id: throwing-weapon
name: Throwing Weapon
kind: crafting
types: physical
slots: 1
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Thrown and hitting, its Category and Qualities apply.
# What it does, for the Effects on its Item's sheet: its Effects line as printed, word for
# word, cut into one line to an effect, each opening with its tag as the rulebook writes one.
summary: >
  [Passive]: If this Weapon hits an Opponent with the use of the Throw Maneuver, apply the
  effects of its Weapon Category and any qualifying Weapon Qualities.
text: >
  Throwing Weapon: This Weapon is perfectly balanced for throwing, allowing it to fly further
  and straighter.
  –Weapon Type: Physical
  –Prerequisites: N/A
  –Quality Slots: 1
  –Effects: If this Weapon hits an Opponent with the use of the Throw Maneuver, apply the
  effects of its Weapon Category and any qualifying Weapon Qualities.

---

# "If this Weapon hits", by the table's ruling: nothing of it on the Strike - not its Size, not the
# Weapon Penalty, not what its Effects add there - and its Size nowhere. Once it hits, the rest:
# its Wound, what it ignores of the target's, Staggering, Lasting Wounds, Breaker, Dimension
# Blade's cost.
[passive]
weapon.throwing = true;
